  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Rules of debit and credit"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Under the accounting equation approach: assets and expenses (including losses and drawings) increase on the debit side and decrease on the credit side. Liabilities, capital and revenues (including gains) increase on the credit side and decrease on the debit side.",
    "kn": "ಆಸ್ತಿ ಮತ್ತು ವೆಚ್ಚ ಹೆಚ್ಚಾದರೆ ಡೆಬಿಟ್, ಕಡಿಮೆಯಾದರೆ ಕ್ರೆಡಿಟ್. ಹೊಣೆಗಾರಿಕೆ, ಬಂಡವಾಳ ಮತ್ತು ಆದಾಯ ಹೆಚ್ಚಾದರೆ ಕ್ರೆಡಿಟ್, ಕಡಿಮೆಯಾದರೆ ಡೆಬಿಟ್."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Assets ↑ Dr, ↓ Cr"
    },
    {
     "en": "Expenses and losses ↑ Dr"
    },
    {
     "en": "Liabilities and capital ↑ Cr"
    },
    {
     "en": "Revenues and gains ↑ Cr"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Under the accounting equation approach: assets and expenses (including losses and drawings) increase on the debit side and decrease on the credit side. Liabilities, capital and revenues (including gains) increase on the credit side and decrease on the debit side.",
    "kn": "ಆಸ್ತಿ ಮತ್ತು ವೆಚ್ಚ ಹೆಚ್ಚಾದರೆ ಡೆಬಿಟ್, ಕಡಿಮೆಯಾದರೆ ಕ್ರೆಡಿಟ್. ಹೊಣೆಗಾರಿಕೆ, ಬಂಡವಾಳ ಮತ್ತು ಆದಾಯ ಹೆಚ್ಚಾದರೆ ಕ್ರೆಡಿಟ್, ಕಡಿಮೆಯಾದರೆ ಡೆಬಿಟ್."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "problem": {
    "en": "State which account is debited and which is credited: (a) bought machinery for cash ₹50,000; (b) paid salary ₹12,000; (c) received interest ₹2,000; (d) took a bank loan ₹1,00,000."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "(a) Machinery (asset ↑) Dr; Cash (asset ↓) Cr."
    },
    {
     "en": "(b) Salary (expense ↑) Dr; Cash (asset ↓) Cr."
    },
    {
     "en": "(c) Cash (asset ↑) Dr; Interest received (revenue ↑) Cr."
    },
    {
     "en": "(d) Cash/Bank (asset ↑) Dr; Bank loan (liability ↑) Cr."
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "en": "(a) Machinery Dr/Cash Cr (b) Salary Dr/Cash Cr (c) Cash Dr/Interest Cr (d) Cash Dr/Loan Cr"
   },
   "narration": {
    "en": "Let us work this out step by step. State which account is debited and which is credited: (a) bought machinery for cash ₹50,000; (b) paid salary ₹12,000; (c) received interest ₹2,000; (d) took a bank loan ₹1,00,000."
   }
